<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">António I of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1661">1661</a>–<a href="/years/1665">1665</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as António I Vita a Nkanga, Mvita a Nkanga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">António I Vita a Nkanga was mwenekongo of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a> from 1661 until his death at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mbwila">Battle of Mbwila</a> in 1665. Elected after the death of Garcia II, he sought to remove the Portuguese from the region, sending envoys to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in vain and turning to Kongo's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbundu">Mbundu</a> allies in Matamba and the kingdoms of Dembos and Mbwila. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> of Portugal ordered the seizure of Kongo's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mines in 1663, António denied that the mines existed. A succession dispute in Mbwila brought both sides to battle, where he was killed leading 400 swordsmen; his death without an heir opened a civil war between the houses of Kinlaza and Kimpanzu, and the kingdom took forty years to be reunited.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-i-of-kongo.jpg" alt="António I of Kongo" width="281" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Affricoll9 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Esteban_de_Dorantes_the_Explorer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mbwila">Battle of Mbwila</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p></section>
